'.agent_tasks/four-lenses-cli-textual_mixins/README.md', 'content': "# Four 
Lenses Bug Report: src/henchman/cli/textual_mixins.py\n## Date: 
2025-03-18T10:15:00Z\n## Bug Summary\nRace condition in tool confirmation future
cleanup where `_cleanup_confirm_futures()` can cancel futures while they're 
being set by callbacks, causing `asyncio.InvalidStateError` or lost 
confirmations.\n\n## Lens\nPhase 2: State & Side Effects (The Entropy Audit) - 
Shared State mutation without proper synchronization\n\n## Expected vs. 
Observed\n| Expected Behavior | Observed Risk |\n|---|---|\n| Tool confirmation 
futures should be safely cancelled during cleanup without race conditions | 
Concurrent access to `_confirm_futures` dict during cleanup and callback 
execution can cause: 1. `asyncio.InvalidStateError` when trying to set result on
already cancelled future 2. Futures being cancelled while callbacks are trying 
to set results 3. Lost confirmations when futures are popped from dict before 
callbacks can access them |\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `_cleanup_confirm_futures()` 
method iterates over the `_confirm_futures` dict and cancels futures, while 
callbacks from confirmation screens may concurrently try to set results on those
same futures. The cleanup uses `list(futures_dict.keys())` to avoid modification
during iteration, but there's still a TOCTOU race between popping the future and
cancelling it.\n\n## Fix Plan\n1. Use `asyncio.Lock` in 
`_cleanup_confirm_futures()` to synchronize access to the futures dict\n2. Pop 
futures from dict under lock protection before cancelling them\n3. Handle 
`asyncio.InvalidStateError` gracefully when cancelling futures that may have 
already completed\n\n## Status: IN PROGRESS"})

